# T-242: shell scripts MUST stay LF regardless of a committer's local
# core.autocrlf setting — a CRLF shebang line ("#!/usr/bin/env bash\r")
# fails with "bad interpreter" on the Linux deploy runner. Mirrors the
# T-217 lesson (em-dashes broke deploy.yml on Windows) for the opposite
# direction: this repo's contributors are on Windows, its deploy targets
# are Linux.
*.sh text eol=lf

# W-164b: same class for ESM launchers with a shebang (web/scripts/run-prod-verify.mjs,
# lint-ci-gate.mjs, scripts/*.mjs): a CRLF checkout on Windows makes vite fail to strip
# "#!/usr/bin/env node" and every test importing the module dies with
# "Invalid or unexpected token" while node itself and the Linux gate pass.
*.mjs text eol=lf
